# printImage(a 16 x 2 all black TYPE_INT_RGB image)   -- body only
# widthBytes = (16 + 7) / 8 = 2. Two rows, band default 128, so one GS v 0 command.
# xL/xH is the width in BYTES little endian; yL/yH the row count little endian.
1B 61 01                  # ESC a 1     centre
1D 76 30 00 02 00 02 00   # GS v 0 0    raster bit image, mode 0 = normal, 2 bytes wide, 2 rows
FF FF                     # row 0: 16 black dots, a set bit is a black dot
FF FF                     # row 1
1B 61 00                  # ESC a 0     back to left
                          # NOTE: no trailing LF. GS v 0 leaves the position on the next line.
